pnet_sys: tv_usec is a C int on QNX.

pnet_sys picks the type of struct timeval's tv_usec per OS and falls back to
c_long. QNX's suseconds_t is 32-bit on both aarch64 and x86_64, so
duration_to_timeval() does not compile there: "expected i32, found i64".
Put QNX (target_os = "nto") with the systems that use c_int.

Applied to pnet_sys 0.35.0 (the version zenoh-c's Cargo.lock pins) by
ports/zenoh-c/recipe.sh, which points cargo at the patched copy.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/src/unix.rs
+++ b/src/unix.rs
@@ -30,14 +30,16 @@
         target_os = "macos",
         target_os = "ios",
         target_os = "tvos",
-        target_os = "netbsd"
+        target_os = "netbsd",
+        target_os = "nto"
     )))]
     pub type TvUsecType = libc::c_long;
     #[cfg(any(
         target_os = "macos",
         target_os = "ios",
         target_os = "tvos",
-        target_os = "netbsd"
+        target_os = "netbsd",
+        target_os = "nto"
     ))]
     pub type TvUsecType = libc::c_int;
     #[cfg(not(any(target_os = "illumos", target_os = "solaris")))]
